INT. PARKING GARAGE ROOFTOP - BOCCE COURT - DUSK

Astroturf laid over oil-stained concrete. Sodium lights flicker on. A hand-painted sign: "LEVEL 6 BOCCE CLUB."

INES VARGA (60s, windbreaker, clipboard she never writes on) stands at the foul line. Arms folded.

DOV LINDQVIST (17, hoodie, too-big sneakers) rolls a ball. It dies short.

Nobody speaks. Ines marks nothing.

KALANI AKANA (30s, delivery-driver vest still on) crouches by the pallino, measuring with a shoelace.

ROSCOE BAPTISTE (70s, folding chair, thermos) watches from the exit ramp.

INES
(to everyone)
Again. Same lane.

Dov collects the balls. Counts them twice. Rolls again. Short.

KALANI
Twelve inches.

DOV
Eleven.

Kalani shows the shoelace. Dov looks away.

ROSCOE
(to himself)
Wind's up.

There is no wind.

Ines walks to Dov. Takes a ball from his hand. Puts it back in the rack, gently.

INES
Eat something.

DOV
I ate.

She looks at his sneakers. Then at the empty parking spaces below the rail, where no car has come for him.

INES
Kalani, you're up.

Kalani stands. Wipes her palms on the vest. Rolls. The ball kisses the pallino and stops.

Roscoe lifts the thermos in salute. Nobody else reacts.

DOV
(muttering)
Lucky.

KALANI
Heard that.

INES
Last end. Then lights off.

She turns away to the stairwell door. Pauses with her hand on the bar.

INES (CONT'D)
(without turning)
Your dad called the club line.

Dov's hand stops over the rack.

DOV
What did you tell him?

INES
That we're closed.

She exits. The door sighs shut.

Dov picks up a ball. Rolls it. It lands inches from the pallino.

He stares at it. Nobody congratulates him. Kalani quietly hands him the shoelace.
